cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Objects in Focus: datasets and tools for mapping fixations to segmented objects"
message: "If you use this dataset or software, please cite both the software and the paper below."
type: software
authors:
  # Add `orcid:` lines here if you would like ORCIDs in the citation metadata.
  - family-names: Hall
    given-names: Elizabeth H.
  - family-names: Loh
    given-names: Zoe
    affiliation: "University of California, Merced"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ehhall/objects-in-focus"
url: "https://ehhall.github.io/objects-in-focus/"
abstract: >-
  A suite of datasets and tools for mapping eye-movement fixations onto
  objects segmented from cluttered, real-world scenes. Includes 100 fully
  segmented scenes with depth maps, a Python package for fixation-to-object
  mapping and per-object feature extraction, and the object-based attention
  model from Hall & Loh (2025).
keywords:
  - eye tracking
  - object-based attention
  - scene perception
  - image segmentation
  - visual salience
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2025-08-21"
